--- body ---
## Context

Author request 2026-10-29 (in place of a shadow-library source): CORE (core.ac.uk) aggregates full
texts harvested from institutional repositories, including theses and accepted manuscripts that
Unpaywall sometimes misses. Biggest remaining open-access gain after OpenAlex (0013) and the ISBN
reshape (0012).

## Actions
1. Check CORE API v3's current terms first (key registration, rate limits, the DOI lookup form, the
   field that carries a downloadable full-text URL).
2. A `core` source under the contract, accepting DOIs; downloads the full text when it passes the
   PDF check. Placed in the default cascade after the open sources (crossref, unpaywall, openalex,
   hal), before the institutional ones.
3. Key handling as for OpenAlex (0013): `CORE_API_KEY` from the environment, else a key file whose
   path defaults to `~/.config/keys/core.env` and is configurable; never printed. Without a key,
   follow CORE's terms; if refused, `failed` with a reason.
4. Mock all network in tests; one `network`-marked test against the live API; covered by 0009's
   conformance suite.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A DOI with a CORE full text and no Unpaywall copy is fetched on a default install
- [ ] Key read from env, else the configurable key file; never printed
- [ ] Conformance suite covers the source; suite passes
